WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.168
-Our first guest tonight i
an Academy Award-winning actress

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from films
such as "Les Misèèrables,"

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Rachel Getting Married,"
and "The Devil Wears Prada."

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is currently starring
in "Locked Down,"

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is now streaming
on HBO Max.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:17.417 line:92%
-3 million pounds, tax-free.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No consequences.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One for me, one for you,
one for the NHS.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:20.720 line:92%
-You have thought about this

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I need to
go meditate!

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, are you sure they won't
check it in New York?

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.694 line:92%
-Shut up! I need to meditate

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.696 line:92%
-What were you going to say?

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The man who bought
the diamond is bad.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:35.335
He's really bad, and you and I
are good, and the NHS is good.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.136 line:92%
And good is better than bad.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.270 size:75% position:38%
And when I explained
all that to Grandma,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
even she said,
"Well, yeah, that's true."

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was a Calvinist,
straight as a rod!

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:48.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unlike me, who is weak
in the face of temptation.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.582 line:92%
-Live wild or die, Linda.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:53.119
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Anne Hathaway!

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Annie?

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey! Hi, Seth!
It's so good to see you.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great to see you as well
-Kind of.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:01.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-As close as we can.

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is really
sort of incredible.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is sort of the first movi
that documents the time

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were living in,
in early 2020.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is when
the movie takes place.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.540 line:92%
All the characters are livin

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.209 size:75% position:38%
through the pandemic
the way we all were.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have been
sort of thrilling

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
and interesting
to be doing that.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, it was exhilarating,
the whole thing.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, the --
'Cause I feel like some people

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
started smoking again
during lockdown.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some people started
drinking with lunch.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we just,
like, took our feelings

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.126 line:92%
and made a film about it.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:37.730
And Steve Knight wrote thi
script that's so sharp and funny

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.799 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and I found cathartic.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:43.369
And it was just -- then I got to
act with Chiwetel Ejiofor,

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.204 line:92%
and Doug Liman was directing

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.941
And all of it just felt like
we probably shouldn't do it,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.242 size:84% position:42% line:92%
but I'm so glad we did.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.010
-Obviously a couple things
you guys were up against.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:55.782
One, were, you know, the ver
intense protocols that we have

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.983 line:92%
when we're shooting films now.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.752 line:92%
And this was shot in London.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also you shot it
very quickly.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it safe to assume that
18 days is the shortest amount

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
of time you've ever worked o
a feature film?

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Certainly when there was
180 pages of dialogue to film.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was -- I've never done
a 180-page script.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:16.803 line:92%
Normally they're about 120

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have about four months
to shoot it.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
This one was
a little bit different.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:25.011 size:88% position:44%
-I'm lucky enough to be
friends with Doug Liman,

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.280 size:75% position:38%
who raves about you,
it should be noted.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.217
-Aw.
-He is, I assume, the right kind

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.954
of director for this "seat o
your pants"-style filming.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For this what kind of pants
Oh, seat of your pants!

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.926
I thought you said seed of
your pants, and I was like

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You know a very different sid
of Doug than I do."

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He wears some
pretty seedy pants.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:45.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"He's got a huge heart."
I just --

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is -- I don't think
I would have said yes

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:52.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
to anyone else, but he has -
he's so inspiring,

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.406 line:92%
and he takes these risks.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:57.177
I mean, you know, he's about
to go into space with Tom Cruise

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
and make a movie
where he's shooting in space

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he just --
he has these ideas.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when he hears someone sa
something's impossible,

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
he wants to show them
how it's not.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.322 line:92%
And I just love him to pieces.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:11.658 size:84% position:42%
-It's true that he's
going to space to shoot

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
a movie with Tom Cruise,
and for those who don't know

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.629 line:92%
he shot "Bourne Identity" and --

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.499 size:75% position:38%
-"Edge of Tomorrow."
-"Edge of Tomorrow."

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's this
incredible filmmaker.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.736 size:88% position:44%
And yet, if you ever saw
the inside of his car,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:27.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
which looks like a garbage can
you would think,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:30.243
"I will not -- I will not pu
my life in this man's hands,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he gets results.
He gets results."

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.948 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's wonderful.

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:37.250
It was one of those things where
we were doing -- we all --

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, it was such a really
hard year for everybody.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:44.791
And it felt so incredible
to be a part of something

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
that not only just
employed people,

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:48.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
which felt like a really great
thing to be a part of,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:53.433
but was able to turn all o
this rage and uncertainty

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all of these feelings
that we were all

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:58.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
just kind of fighting our wa
through and turn it

00:03:58.238 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
into something, like I said,
hopefully, cathartic.

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:04.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry, I get nervous
talking to you.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's happening.
Is my neck red yet?

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:11.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-That's the intention.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
We do try to keep people,
especially you.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
We want to keep you
off your axis.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:18.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, you know, you mostly shot
it in an apartment,

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.893
but you also --
and I think it's safe to assume,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
you would never have been able
to shut down Harrods,

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is this famous departmen
store in London

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:29.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you guys got to shoot in,
which must have been

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:32.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
both exciting but incredibly
eerie to be in a place

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:34.941
that is usually so bustling with
human beings.

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:36.776 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It was that.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.344 line:92%
It was -- you know, it just --

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
it just kind of added to
the surreality of everything

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:44.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it sort of reminded me
of when I was a kid

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.953 size:88% position:44%
and my parents used to
bring us to FAO Schwarz,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we couldn't afford anythin
in FAO Schwarz.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
My parents told us
it was a toy museum.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.193
And that's what being in Harrods
at night was like.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was kind of like the museum
of super fancy stuff.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. That's -- Man, I ti
my cap to your parents.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's genius.
-Very clever.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had a lot of work-arounds
for stuff like that.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There are some, maybe clich
is not the right word,

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:10.843
but things that I think all of
us have maybe at least thought

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
about doing
during this difficult year

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.780 line:92%
that happened in the film.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.581 size:75% position:38%
So I want to ask you
if these are things

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you've ever done
in real life.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-And I will answer as well

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.656 size:81% position:41%
-Scream into a pillow.
Yes or no, real life?

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So many times.
-Really?

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:28.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So many times. That actuall
wasn't in the movie.

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.730
We had done a couple takes
and then I turned to Doug,

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said, "Can I --
I don't want to tell you

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I'm going to do,
but can I just try something?"

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Yeah,"
and I grabbed the pillow,

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:39.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I just screamed as hard,
like, loud and as hard

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
as I could into it,
and then I did this scene.

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at the end,
Doug's eyes were really wide

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he just went,
"Oh, do that again.

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:46.112 line:92%
Yeah, that, do that again.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:49.148
In the early days of lockdown,
I -- you know, we were all -

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:52.085
I mean, I'm still overwhelmed,
but especially in the beginnin

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:55.421 size:84% position:42%
when, I mean, there was
just a lot to process.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:58.224
I would need to release, but I
didn't want to scare my kids

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I screamed into
a pillow a lot.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:02.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See, I think I just screa
too loud

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.896 line:92%
when something minor happens

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:07.867
Like the other day, I got a very
small splinter on the banister

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:11.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
and screamed really loud,
and then my wife very calmly

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
explained to me that
it's upsetting to the kids

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:17.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I broke a bowl
that was very meaningful,

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I started to cry
way too hard.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Adam had to come up to me,
and he's like,

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Honey, you are legit
frightening the children.

00:06:23.116 --> 00:06:25.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to pull it together,
honey."

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:28.721 size:78% position:39%
-Have you ever stayed
in pajamas all day?

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course.
-Yeah.

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:31.190 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Of course.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did do my best
to try to get dressed

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:36.596
just because I'm somebody,
if I don't kind of start my day,

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:39.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
get myself out of bed,
start my routine, I can get --

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:40.700 line:92%
it can get a little mushy.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.902 size:81% position:41%
So I found it was good
for my mental health

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
to put on something
with a zipper.

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I think that's right.
What about tie-dye?

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:50.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you tie-dye any clothe
during the pandemic?

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:50.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I didn't.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
But going back to Doug Liman
for a second,

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, we -- like you said,
we shot this whole thing -

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:58.918
well, not by the seed of you
pants, the seat of our pants

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:04.223
But we didn't have a look fo
the final scene of the movie

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they'd been in lockdow
for a very long time.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:09.796
And, like, with -- I think i
was something like 18 hour

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
before we had to
shoot the scene, I said,

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:12.865 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Oh, what about tie-dye?

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody was tie-dyeing
during this time.

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:16.068
Wouldn't it be funny if she'
wearing a tie-dyed shirt?"

00:07:16.068 --> 00:07:19.572
And our poor costume designer,
who had done such an amazing job

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was so exhausted,
single-handedly dressing

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.776 size:78% position:39%
everybody, just said,
"I just -- I just --

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very exhausted
and I don't think I can."

00:07:25.812 --> 00:07:28.381
And Doug raised his hand.
He's like, "I'll do it!

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:29.882 line:92%
I'll tie-dye a bunch of shirts."

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:32.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he spent his Sunday
tie-dyeing shirts,

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
came in with
a dozen of them and that's -

00:07:34.487 --> 00:07:35.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I wore one of them
in the movie.

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.623 size:81% position:41% line:92%
So I didn't. Doug did.

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:39.659 line:92%
-He is a Jack-of-all-trades.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
No one can say otherwise
about our friend Doug Liman.

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He can tie-dye.
He goes into space.

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
He does it all.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:44.464 --> 00:07:46.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Makes films in lockdown.
-Hey, it's always

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
such a delight to see you.
Congrats on the film.

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:50.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really do hope next time
it's in person.

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:54.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that would be a dream -
that would be incredible.

